"""OptiLock-derived preset data -- GENERATED, do not hand-edit.

Provenance (read 2026-11-05, repository commit 77489664c3e2367c486a81ffd62b0f3f28d3454d):

  https://github.com/dacooderr/OptiLock
  "OptiLock FPS Config (Recommended)" / "OptiLock Potato Config" /
  "OptiLock Ultra Potato Config" / "OptiLock Community Config"

OptiLock is GPL-3.0. Its ``gameinfo.gi`` files embed a full ``ConVars``
block, which is the only public surface where those values appear, and those
values are what this module carries. Treat it as GPL-3.0 material: SpeedyLock
is therefore distributed under GPL-3.0 as a whole (see LICENSE.md).

What was extracted: every ``name "value"`` pair inside each tier's ConVars
block, plus each tier's ``video.txt``. Display and hardware keys (resolution,
monitor, gamma, render scale, deviceid) were dropped on the way in, because
SpeedyLock never writes those regardless of who supplied them.

The four tiers are far less different than their names suggest: the ConVars
block is identical across Recommended/Potato/Ultra except for a handful of
rows, and ``video.txt`` differs in four keys. Those deltas are stored as
overrides rather than four full copies.
"""

